<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46269" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">succĭdŭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		1. succido, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>sinking down</i>, <i>sinking</i>, <i>failing</i> (<b>poet.</b>).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					13, 24</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">poples,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					M. 10, 458</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gradus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 4, 661</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flammae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 10, 116</span></i>
			 et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">benedictio,</span>”
				<i>faltering</i>, <i>trembling</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 7, 6 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> =
			succidaneus (late Lat.), Ven. Misc. 4, 25, 10.</div>
